{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"74c12a05-9738-4abc-81d7-e0decf6a7190","step_index":6,"state":"DONE","step_type":"agent_response","text_delta":"{\"_kritt_extractor_helper\":true,\"results\":[],\"stub\":true,\"stub_explanation\":\"The ticket ownership and existence checks in Raffle.refundTickets operate as intended without vulnerability. In each iteration of the bounded batch loop, ownerOf(ticketId) reverts with ERC721NonexistentToken if a ticket ID was never minted, was previously refunded, or appears more than once in the caller-supplied ticketIds array (since _burn(ticketId) clears ERC-721 ownership immediately on the first occurrence). The subsequent msg.sender != owner check strictly enforces direct bearer-ticket ownership and reverts the caller's own transaction with NotTicketOwner if any supplied ticket is owned by another address. Because callers select their own ticketIds array and _burn performs no external calls, this revert path prevents double-refunding and unauthorized claims without introducing denial-of-service or state-corruption vectors.\"}\n","duration_seconds":20.729731,"usage":{"input_tokens":9931,"output_tokens":1659,"thinking_tokens":1459,"cache_read_tokens":20613,"total_tokens":11590}}}
